Chapter: CodexZigHarness

Section: Halt

 The driver this stands in for does not emit when the bag has errors:
 opening.codex:1676-1678 prints the codegen error header and the notices,
 and then `if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED:
 errors in bag; no IR emitted"`. Without this gate a file reading `this is
 not codex at all` produces 36,697 bytes of plausible zig and exit 0, and so
 does a program calling a function that does not exist -- measured, both. For
 a tool handed to other people, the first thing they will feed it is a
 program with a mistake in it.

 The bags are the ones the driver merges, reached from what the frontend
 already binds: lex errors from `toks.errors` (opening.codex:449 wraps the
 same list), the parse bag from `doc.parse-bag` (:485), the resolve bag from
 `rr.bag`, and the type checker's from `cr.state.bag` -- which is what
 `check-bag0` at :620 merges. The PRINTERS are not reachable: they live in
 opening.codex, which cannot be bundled beside a harness defining `opening`,
 so this prints the count and the first error rather than the driver's full
 report.

 CODEGEN-HALTED is the marker build.py refuses on by name, in the two
 places a transpile is read: the bare-metal arm and the self arm.

  czg-halted : List Diagnostic -> Text
  czg-halted (es) =
   let n = list-length es
   in let e0 = list-at es 0
   in "CODEGEN-HALTED: " & show n & " error(s); no zig emitted; first CDX" & show (e0.code) & " " & (e0.message) & "\n"

 THE NON-ERROR DIAGNOSTICS GO TO STDOUT, and until 2026-08-30 they went
 nowhere. This harness merged the driver's four bags and then asked one
 predicate, `bag-has-errors`, so on a clean compile every warning and info sat
 in `czg-bag` and was discarded. A driving-screensaver port compiled fifteen
 units through this tool and through the seed, got byte-identical program
 output, and learned only from the seed that it carried ten real CDX3006 name
 collisions -- two definitions of one name in two chapters, four times over.
 It had been green its whole life.

 STDOUT AND NOT print-text, because `print-text` is `std.debug.print`, which is
 stderr -- and stderr is where this tool's OUTPUT goes. `codexzig < prog.codex
 2> prog.zig` is the invocation. A warning printed the ordinary way would land
 inside the emitted zig. `write-binary` is the only route to fd 1 from Codex
 and it takes raw bytes, which is what `text-to-utf8-bytes` in Foreword chapter
 CCE is for -- the symmetric partner of `utf8-bytes-to-text`, already in this
 bundle, so nothing needed to be added to the compiler.

 INFOS ARE COUNTED, NOT PRINTED. Those same fifteen units carried 3,685
 CDX4010 `bounds proven` infos against the ten warnings. Printing every
 non-error would bury the thing worth reading in its own telemetry.

  czg-sev-word : Integer -> Text
  czg-sev-word (s) = if s == sev-warning then "warning" else "notice"

  czg-notice-line : Diagnostic -> Text
  czg-notice-line (d) = "CDX" & show (d.code) & " " & czg-sev-word (d.severity) & ": " & (d.message)

  czg-line-bytes : Text -> List Integer
  czg-line-bytes (t) = list-push (text-to-utf8-bytes t) 10

  czg-notices : List Diagnostic, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  czg-notices (ds) (i) (acc) =
   if i >= list-length ds then acc
   else let d = list-at ds i
   in if (d.severity) == sev-info then czg-notices ds (i + 1) acc
   else czg-notices ds (i + 1) (acc & czg-line-bytes (czg-notice-line d))

  czg-info-count : List Diagnostic, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  czg-info-count (ds) (i) (n) =
   if i >= list-length ds then n
   else let d = list-at ds i
   in if (d.severity) == sev-info then czg-info-count ds (i + 1) (n + 1)
   else czg-info-count ds (i + 1) n

  czg-report : DiagnosticBag -> List Integer
  czg-report (b) =
   let ds = bag-diagnostics b
   in let body = czg-notices ds 0 []
   in let n = czg-info-count ds 0 0
   in if n == 0 then body
   else body & czg-line-bytes ("codexzig: " & show n & " info diagnostics not shown")

Section: Roots

 opening.codex:1316, copied because that chapter cannot ride along.

  czg-emit-roots : List Text
  czg-emit-roots = ["opening", "vb-capacity-auto", "vb-read-auto", "vb-write-auto", "fat16-servicer-read", "fat16-servicer-write"]

Section: Driver

 THIS CALLS THE DRIVER; it does not stand in for one. Update 55 split the entry
 point out, so `Chapter: Opening` is bundlable by a subject supplying its own
 `opening`, and `compile-frontend-cdx` does lex, parse, desugar, scope, check,
 lower, the IR pipeline, resolve and the lambda lift behind one call.

 What that replaces is thirty lines of copied phase order and deck arithmetic,
 and the copy is where every defect of 2026-09-04 lived: a `lower-chapter` call
 left bare when Update 55 gave it a caller-extent requirement, a ceiling pinned
 to 0 because no phase here was wrapped in an extent, and no lowering scratch
 region at all. The driver has always had those; a copy has them only until the
 next Update moves them. The ladder made this same change at Update 55.

 `cdx-ir` AND NOT `ir`: `compile-frontend-cdx` returns the lifted chapter in
 `cdx-ir` and deliberately blanks `ir` to a defs-less IRChapter, so reading the
 obvious field yields a program with no definitions in it.

 The bag is the driver's own, which subsumes the three checks this harness used
 to run itself -- shadowed builtins, cross-chapter collisions and a duplicate
 entry point are all merged into `fe.bag` by `compile-checked`.

  opening : [Console, FileSystem] Nothing = act
    src <- read-file-uni "/dev/stdin"
    let mountain-base = init-phase-allocator
    in let deck-base = __heap-save
    in let deck-set = __deck-set deck-base
    in let deck-adv = __heap-advance 536870912
    in let fe = compile-frontend-cdx src "Codex_Codex" compile-flags-default
    in if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then print-text (czg-halted (bag-errors (fe.bag)))
    else let ir-text = emit-ir-chapter (ir-prune-unreachable-roots (fe.cdx-ir) czg-emit-roots) (fe.text-meta) (fe.type-defs)
    in let parsed = parse-ir-chapter ir-text
    in act
      write-binary (czg-report (fe.bag))
      print-text (emit-zig-chapter (parsed.chapter) (parsed.type-defs))
    end
  end
